\ A definition made inside a called quotation stays legal at binary runtime. The interpreter
\ gives the quotation a transient lexical frame, so the binding is exempt from the collision
\ guards and pops with the frame. An interpreter-free binary pushes no transient frame; the
\ definition lands in the durable entry frame, runs the guards, and a fresh name passes them.
\
\ The helper is deliberately never called: a body that calls its own nested definition cannot be
\ AOT-compiled, so a call would turn this pin into a build failure rather than a
\ runtime-legality check.

[ helper: ( -- n ) [ 42 ] ; ] call

"after" print-line
